# Codex Phase 4 — Real DonutSMP Session Capture

Phase 3 is complete.

Current state:

* semantic GUI learning
* changed-slot detection
* guarded clicks
* two-stage purchase validation
* 24 passing tests
* lint/typecheck/build/Compose passing
* hot-path benchmark ~0.0167 ms/iteration

Do not redesign the architecture.

The next goal is to connect the system to a real authenticated Minecraft client and record the actual DonutSMP AH interaction lifecycle.

## Main Goal

Create a client-side bridge that streams structured Minecraft state to our backend.

The owner will:

1. launch Minecraft;
2. authenticate manually;
3. join DonutSMP manually;
4. enable the client bridge.

After that, the bridge should automatically send:

```text
screen open/close
screen title
slot updates
item id
display name
lore
quantity
relevant metadata/NBT
inventory changes
chat messages
connection state
player-visible balance if observable
mouse/slot actions performed by the owner
```

Use structured data, not screenshots.

## Client Bridge

Prefer a Fabric client mod.

It should connect locally to the existing `ExternalGameClientAdapter` using WebSocket.

Implement:

```text
Fabric client
    ↓
localhost WebSocket
    ↓
ExternalGameClientAdapter
    ↓
discovery + recorder
```

Authentication to Minecraft remains manual.


## Observation Mode First

The first real session must run in:

```text
OBSERVE_ONLY
```

The backend may learn and record states but must not send financial clicks.

Record:

```text
GUI snapshots
changed slots
manual clicks
GUI transitions
chat results
inventory changes
timings
```

Persist sessions so they can be replayed later.

## Learn the Actual DonutSMP Flow

Record the owner manually performing:

```text
/ah
→ browse first page
→ next page
→ previous page
→ refresh if available
→ click a listing
→ inspect purchase confirmation
→ cancel purchase
```

Then record one controlled real purchase of a very cheap item only after the owner explicitly enables financial execution.

Also record the actual selling flow:

```text
select owned item
→ initiate AH sell
→ set price
→ confirm
→ verify listing exists
→ cancel or allow sale
```

Do not guess command names or slot numbers.

Learn them from observed actions and state transitions.

